<h1>Bind Views - Absolute</h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Windows &gt; Bind Views &gt; Absolute</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">or by pressing</span> <b><span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Shift + B</b></span></b><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Open two or more documents and tile them horizontally or vertically.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span lang="EN-GB">When enabled</span> <span class="Command">Bind Views - Absolute</span> <span lang="EN-GB">will cause all open windows to display the same visible region and to update all views simultaneously according to the active window. This means that all commands (</span><span class="Command">Zoom</span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span class="Command">Rotate</span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span class="Command">Pan</span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span class="Command">change light direction</span><span lang="EN-GB">, etc.) applied to the active window will have the same effect on all other windows.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is applicable for different documents. When this mode is enabled the command is marked with a tick and a right chain icon appears at the top left corner of every window:</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="Images/bindview_absolute_icon.gif" width="376px" height="496px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Call</span> <span class="Command">Bind Views - None</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to disable it. The state of</span> <span class="Command">Bind Views - Absolute</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is not stored so next time when you run KUBE will be disabled.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span class="Command">Bind Views - Absolute</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>useful</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">when you want to compare two objects scanned at the same site or if you have one scan that is post-processed in different ways and saved in separate documents.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: Do not apply this command if the objects from the different documents are too far away from each other according to the global co-ordinate system because you will loose the objects from the other viewports. In this case fit the objects of interest in the windows and enable <a href="Bind_Views_Relative.htm">Bind Views - Relative</a> mode.</span></p>
